[Music]  this women's history month our series  changing the game is profiling  extraordinary women making an impact and  on now and on the future this morning  we're talking to a beauty entrepreneur  whose e-commerce site supports brands  created by black and brown founders her  name is nikeo grieco she's a co-founder  of 13 loon in style magazine listen to  this named her one of 50 women making  the world a better place in 2022. one  that's the list you want to be on the ko  13 loon represents more than 140  different beauty brands 90 of them are  founded by entrepreneurs who are black  indigenous or people of color 13 loon  recently partnered with jcpenney to  bring those products to 650 stores  nationwide the ko grieco joins us this  morning you are on a roll my friend  congratulations save yourself a round of  applause i say bravo to you because a  recent report says that black female  entrepreneurs you know this received  less than one percent of venture capital  investments less than one percent  so when you when you launched your line  what were some of the challenges you  faced what made you say i can do this  yeah you know so i launched a beauty  line 20 years ago uh called niko beauty  based on my family beauty secrets from  kenya my grandmother was a coffee farmer  my grandfather was a medicine man so was  inspired to bring those beauty secrets  here and you know i've been raising  money on and off for the last 20 years  and what i will say is that access to  capital has been one of my biggest  challenges but i have hope because uh  the venture world is starting to look a  little different and so while there's  much work to do  um it's getting better and better you  believe in the 9010 rule what does that  mean yes so at 13 loon we adopted what  we call our 9010 rule which is 90 of all  the brands we carry are created by  people of color who make products for  people of all colors and 10 are  dedicated to fostering ally ship and so  we call an ally brand a brand that you  know may not be black or brown founded  but has long been looking to serve that  consumer long before uh the racial  reckoning and then to debunk the myth  that black and brown people just make  products for black and brown people yeah  we know that  yeah yeah we do know that so you make  products for every every single person  yeah it's it's black and brown by poc  for all as well as having ally brands  because we want to be truly truly  inclusive and that means including  everyone you know when it comes to the  ratings they say black shoppers spend a  lot of money they sure did a lot of  money on beauty product products but  many people don't believe that the  beauty industry is kept up when it comes  to representation do you think that's  true yeah you know i i think that you  know in creating 13 luna it gave us an  opportunity and a responsibility you  know i know firsthand what it's like  being a beauty founder and and trying to  get representation in big retailers and  and you know being able to serve a  larger audience and so we wanted to make  13 loon a place to make your beauty  shopping more meaningful and make it  easier for people to to do the right  thing beauty is universal it's fun we  all love it but it's also a way that we  can help to build generational wealth  through the lens of beauty and in our  black and brown communities and and and  celebrate these global beauty secrets  and give these founders who are  incredible making non-toxic amazing  ingredients makeup in all shade ranges  um hair products that work on all hair  types the opportunity to be seen so here  here's here's your pitch uh niko what  what do you bring that nobody else does  when it comes to your line what is it i  think that we really truly bring the  first of its kind truly inclusive beauty  retail platform and now stores within  our 13 loon stores at jcpenney um we all  want to see ourselves reflected on the  shelf and we you know what you see you  do and and so i think that we're  inspiring the next generation of beauty  founders to know they can do it too but  also giving these brands the opportunity  to serve a wider audience to uh be  amplified and celebrated and and share  their products with them what does 13  loon mean so 13 my i haven't heard of 13  lou my my makeup artist who i think does  a good job yeah you should see me  without this i love it all speckled up i  thought it was 13 line and she said no  13 what does it mean yeah so 13's always  been one of my favorite numbers i grew  up first generation american so i never  knew it to be you know sort of bad luck  which i think is talked about a lot in  this country and then when i started to  research the number 13 realize that it's  an it's a number of the divine feminine  it's a powerful number and loon means  moon moon and 13 full moon mateo rico  nakayo grico thank you congrats you  thanks for having me

